  "narrative": {
    "intro": "California federal contracting through FY2027 to date shows a concentrated set of awards and a sharp year-over-year decline. Total obligations in FY2027 to date are $1.8B. Award activity in FY2027 to date includes 8,351 awards with an average award size of $218K. Obligations are down 96.9% year over year. Historical annual obligations provide context: FY22 totaled $58.4B, FY23 totaled $63.1B, FY24 totaled $63.2B, FY25 totaled $63.2B, and FY26 totaled $59.1B. Research and development categories lead industry spending in FY2027 to date with multiple R&D NAICS entries totaling $842M and $254M in the top two R&D lines. The Department of Energy and the National Aeronautics and Space Administration lead agency buying with $836M and $419M respectively. LAWRENCE LIVERMORE NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC and CALIFORNIA INSTITUTE OF TECHNOLOGY lead vendor obligations with $550M and $206M respectively. Readers should treat FY2027 totals as partial because FY2027 to date is a fiscal year to date figure.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What is the spending picture in California for FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "Total obligations in FY2027 to date are $1.8B and award activity counts 8,351 awards with an average award size of $218K. Obligations are down 96.9% year over year, reflecting that FY2027 to date totals are partial fiscal year numbers. Historical annual obligations show multiyear scale: FY22 was $58.4B, FY23 was $63.1B, FY24 was $63.2B, FY25 was $63.2B, and FY26 was $59.1B. Research and development industries account for a large share of FY2027 to date obligations, led by R&D entries totaling $842M and $254M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors dominate FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Energy is the top buying agency with $836M, followed by the National Aeronautics and Space Administration with $419M and the Department of Veterans Affairs with $362M. LAWRENCE LIVERMORE NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC leads vendors with $550M, followed by CALIFORNIA INSTITUTE OF TECHNOLOGY with $206M and THE REGENTS OF THE UNIVERSITY OF CALIFORNIA with $162M. Additional notable agencies include the General Services Administration with $53.7M and the Department of Justice with $47M. Additional notable vendors include THE LELAND STANFORD JUNIOR UNIVERSITY with $132M and ELEVATED TECHNOLOGIES SERVICES, LLC with $57M."
      }
    ]
  },
